1.1.0: camera/film compatibility model

Cameras now declare which film processes they accept (slide, C-41
negative, black-and-white, Polaroid integral, peel-apart pack), and
autochrome and technicolor-3strip are classified as sealed processes
that take no film at all - the plate or dye-transfer process is the
medium. The CLI refuses incompatible pairings with an explanation
(inferring a film's process from its library location, with stem
overrides for instant stocks; out-of-library cubes are never blocked),
and --any-film bypasses every check, because darkrooms allowed
deliberate mismatches and the engine should not be more dogmatic than a
lab. The famous mismatch has first-class support instead: slide in
negative chemistry is what --develop cross emulates, alongside the
measured Cross-processed CLUT family.

The web rebuilds the film dropdown per camera to show only compatible
families and disables it entirely for sealed processes; 'cameras',
'describe' and the help panel print a films: line per camera. The
README documents the full model and its escape hatches.

Core: pj_preset_accepts_film() and pj_preset_film_processes() with a
per-preset process bitmask; truth-table tests across all tiers.
